# Returns the number of error rows collected for this run.
# NOT deduplicated - $handleError adds every error it is handed, filtered
# only by cIgnoreCodes. The word unique stood here until 2026-09-01 and
# described a condition that had already been removed; the dead # End If
# under the $add was its scar. A comment that outlives its code is worse
# than no comment: it was read as a promise and sent a search the wrong way.
If cErrors.$linecount.$cando
	# rows with errcode danger are findings of the danger scan, not errors of the run
	Calculate vCount as 0
	For vN from 1 to cErrors.$linecount step 1
		If (cErrors.[vN].errcode<>'danger')&(cErrors.[vN].errcode<>'ignored')
			Calculate vCount as vCount+1
		End If
	End For
	Quit method vCount
Else
	Quit method 0
End If